hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2905","Narrated to us Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Ala', narrated to us Sufyan, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim. (Another chain) Narrated to us 'Ali ibn Khashram, who informed us Ibn 'Uyaynah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim. (Another chain) Narrated to us Abu Musa, who narrated to us Ibn 'Uyaynah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from 'A'ishah (RA), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sacrificed on behalf of his wives with a cow.\n\nThis is the wording of Abd al-Jabbar and 'Ali. As for Abu Musa, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said to her, \You menstruated at Sarif before entering Makkah"," so he said to her"," 'Perform what the pilgrims perform except that you do not circumambulate the House.'\"" She said: When we were in Mina"," I was brought meat of a cow"," so I said"," \""What is this?\"" They said"," \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sacrificed on behalf of his wives with cows.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
